WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:06.500
Eight major document leaks from 2014 to 2023 exposed more than 268,000 offshore entities across dozens of jurisdictions.

00:00:06.500 --> 00:00:11.200
912 Canadian entities in Panama Papers alone. More than 3,000 Canadians in Paradise Papers.

00:00:11.200 --> 00:00:16.800
CRA found 76 million dollars in unpaid taxes. Zero criminal prosecutions in Canada.

00:00:16.800 --> 00:00:22.400
Now the Carney government has defunded FINTRAC while Brookfield routes pension funds offshore.

00:00:22.400 --> 00:00:34.000
LuxLeaks. November 5, 2014. 28,000 pages of confidential tax rulings leaked from PricewaterhouseCoopers Luxembourg. 340 multinational companies secured secret tax deals, paying effective rates below 1 percent.

00:00:34.000 --> 00:00:47.500
Swiss Leaks. February 8, 2015. More than 60,000 leaked files from HSBC's Swiss private banking arm. CRA identified 1,859 Canadian HSBC clients with accounts totalling 5.7 billion dollars. Only one criminal prosecution resulted.

00:00:47.500 --> 00:01:02.000
Panama Papers. April 3, 2016. 11.5 million documents leaked from Mossack Fonseca. 214,488 offshore entities. 912 Canadian entities. CRA identified nearly 900 Canadians. Only 5 investigations opened. Zero criminal charges.

00:01:02.000 --> 00:01:15.000
Paradise Papers. November 5, 2017. 13.4 million documents from Appleby law firm. 7 of Canada's 8 major pension funds using offshore tax havens. Stephen Bronfman, Liberal Party chief fundraiser, linked to Cayman Islands trust. Zero investigations.

00:01:15.000 --> 00:01:27.000
FinCEN Files. September 20, 2020. More than 2,100 suspicious activity reports. 2 trillion dollars in suspicious transactions. Canadian banks including TD, BMO, and Scotiabank processed hundreds of millions in flagged transactions. No enforcement action.

00:01:27.000 --> 00:01:38.000
Pandora Papers. October 3, 2021. 11.9 million documents from 14 offshore service providers. 35 current and former world leaders named. Still zero criminal prosecutions.

00:01:38.000 --> 00:01:49.500
Suisse Secrets. February 20, 2022. Data on more than 18,000 accounts at Credit Suisse holding over 100 billion Swiss francs. Credit Suisse collapsed in 2023 and was absorbed by UBS. No Canadian regulatory action.

00:01:49.500 --> 00:02:01.000
Cyprus Confidential. November 2023. Cyprus became Europe's primary money laundering hub for Russian oligarchs. Canadian entities with cross-border ties were documented. Canada took no action.

00:02:01.000 --> 00:02:14.000
After eight major leaks across a decade, the Canada Revenue Agency identified 76 million dollars in unpaid taxes. They cannot confirm whether they collected a single dollar. Globally, 1.36 billion in recovered taxes. Canada: zero.

00:02:14.000 --> 00:02:28.000
In 2026, the Carney Government and Brookfield began routing Canadian pension funds through offshore accounts. Carney slashed FINTRAC funding. The PM holds 6.8 million in Brookfield options. Brookfield manages 1 trillion globally. FINTRAC budget cut 12 percent. 47 analyst positions eliminated.

00:02:28.000 --> 00:02:40.000
Twelve years. Eight leaks. Zero prosecutions. All data sourced from ICIJ Offshore Leaks Database, CRA reports, CBC, Globe and Mail, OCCRP, and FINTRAC annual reports.
